              "cwe": "CWE-294",
              "impact": "Any party that obtains a copied room-scoped reconnect secret can repeatedly take over an active session without knowing any password or completing the original join flow. In the validated proof of concept, replaying a copied player token seized that player's identity and evicted the legitimate socket, while replaying a copied `hostKey` seized host control, allowed unauthorized `host:config` changes, and displaced the original host; the same copied secrets remained valid from a third socket.",
              "technical_analysis": "The room host and player rejoin paths both rely on long-lived browser-stored bearer secrets and do not rotate them after a successful takeover.\n\nThe host client persists `{ code, hostKey }` in `sessionStorage` and reuses it automatically:\n\n```javascript title=public/js/host.js startLineNumber=40 endLineNumber=65\nconst saved = JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('mc_host') || 'null');\n\nsocket.on('connect', async () => {\n  const s = await syncClock(socket, 6);\n  state.offset = s.offset;\n  if (state.code && state.hostKey) {\n    socket.emit('host:rejoin', { code: state.code, hostKey: state.hostKey }, () => {});\n  } else if (saved && !state.code) {\n    socket.emit('host:rejoin', saved, (res) => {\n      if (res && res.ok) {\n        state.code = res.code;\n        state.hostKey = saved.hostKey;\n        state.config = res.config;\n        enterLobbyUi(res);\n      }\n    });\n  }\n});\n```\n\nThe player client persists `mc_pid_<ROOM>` and `mc_reconnect_<ROOM>` in `localStorage` and reuses them on join/reconnect:\n\n```javascript title=public/js/player.js startLineNumber=43 endLineNumber=54\nconst storedPid = localStorage.getItem(`mc_pid_${code}`);\nconst storedToken = localStorage.getItem(`mc_reconnect_${code}`);\nconst canReconnect = Boolean(storedPid && storedToken);\nsocket.emit('player:join', {\n  code,\n  name,\n  playerId: canReconnect ? storedPid : null,\n  reconnectToken: canReconnect ? storedToken : null,\n}, (res) => enterRoom(res, code));\n```\n\nOn the server, `host:rejoin` authorizes control solely by room code plus the stored `hostKey`, then moves host authority to the new socket without rotating that secret:\n\n```javascript title=server/sockets.js startLineNumber=198 endLineNumber=224\nsocket.on('host:rejoin', guarded(socket, 'host:rejoin', { limit: 10, ack: true }, ({ code, hostKey } = {}, cb) => {\n  const r = rooms.get(String(code || '').toUpperCase());\n  if (!r || r.hostKey !== hostKey) return cb?.(failedJoinResponse(failedJoins, socket));\n  // ...snip...\n  r.hostSocketId = socket.id;\n  // ...snip...\n  cb?.({ ok: true, code: r.code, snapshot: r.snapshot(null), config: r.publicConfig() });\n}));\n```\n\nThe player reconnect path similarly accepts `playerId` plus `reconnectToken`, evicts the previous socket, and then returns the same reconnect token again:\n\n```javascript title=server/room.js startLineNumber=327 endLineNumber=370\nif (playerId && this.players.has(playerId)) {\n  const p = this.players.get(playerId);\n  if (!reconnectTokenMatches(p.reconnectToken, reconnectToken)) {\n    return { error: 'Reconnect credential is invalid or expired.' };\n  }\n  const previousSocketId = p.socketId;\n  if (previousSocketId && previousSocketId !== socket.id) {\n    this.disconnectSocketPlayers(previousSocketId, p.id);\n  }\n  // ...snip...\n  return {\n    ok: true,\n    playerId: p.id,\n    reconnectToken: p.reconnectToken,\n    name: p.name,\n    snapshot: this.snapshot(p.id),\n  };\n}\n```\n\nBecause the same bearer secret survives every successful takeover, possession of a copied value is enough to repeatedly bind fresh sockets to the same host or player identity. The previous socket is evicted, but the credential itself remains valid indefinitely for the life of the room, so the same copied secret can be replayed again from a third socket.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Rotate the host bearer token immediately after every successful `host:rejoin`, return the replacement token in the acknowledgement, and overwrite the browser's stored `mc_host` value with the rotated secret.\n2. Rotate each player's reconnect token immediately after every successful authenticated reconnect, return the replacement token in the join acknowledgement, and persist only the rotated token client-side.\n3. Treat reconnect credentials as one-time or short-lived bearer secrets rather than room-lifetime tokens; if transport reliability requires retry tolerance, keep only a narrowly bounded transition window instead of allowing indefinite replay across successive takeovers.\n4. Add regression tests proving that a copied pre-rejoin host or player token fails after the first successful rejoin, while the freshly returned replacement token still permits the legitimate browser to resume the session.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Create a room as the host and join it as a normal player.\n2. Copy the host browser's `sessionStorage.mc_host` value and the player browser's `localStorage.mc_pid_<ROOM>` plus `localStorage.mc_reconnect_<ROOM>` values.\n3. Open a fresh socket and call `player:join` with the copied room code, `playerId`, and `reconnectToken`.\n4. Observe that the new socket is accepted as the existing player identity and the legitimate player socket immediately loses room access.\n5. Open a third socket and replay the same copied player values again.\n6. Observe that the third socket is again accepted as the same player, proving the reconnect token was not invalidated after the previous takeover.\n7. Open a fresh socket and call `host:rejoin` with the copied room code and `hostKey`.\n8. Observe that the new socket gains host control, can successfully invoke `host:config`, and the original host can no longer do so.\n9. Open a third host socket and replay the same copied `hostKey` again.\n10. Observe that host takeover succeeds again, proving the host secret was not rotated after the prior rejoin.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
